# The FAIR FHGFF3 header development copy under header/ is byte-exact against
# the pinned upstream revision recorded in header/provenance.json
# (scripts/check_header_parity.py). Never convert its line endings: the CRLF
# vectors and the checksummed examples must keep their exact bytes.
header/** -text
header/**/*.gz binary

# The draft FHGM vector set under development/ is byte-exact and checksum-bound:
# development/conformance/manifest.json records a size and SHA-256 per vector, and
# development/examples/model and development/examples/s6k hold the v0.1 fixtures the
# manifest cites in place. Never convert their line endings, and do not open and
# re-save them - regenerate with make_vectors.py / make_fixtures.py instead.
development/conformance/** -text
development/examples/**/*.gff3 -text
